/// JsonMappable — derive `asJson` from a declarative `JsonMapping` (BT-2819).
///
/// A using class implements the class-side `jsonMapping`, and `asJson` is
/// provided: `(JsonMapping forClass: self class) encode: self`. `Json generate:` finds it
/// through the ordinary `asJson` hook (see `JsonRepresentable`), so no runtime
/// change is involved, and nested mapped objects convert recursively.
///
/// A class that `uses: JsonMappable` without defining `class jsonMapping` gets a
/// does-not-understand diagnostic for `jsonMapping` at compile time (an error
/// when warnings are errors, as in the stdlib build). If that diagnostic is not
/// treated as an error, `asJson` (and so `Json generate:`) raises
/// `does_not_understand` at runtime.
///
/// It works on Actors as well as Values (`encode:` reads fields via same-process
/// self-sends, so it does not re-enter the actor).
///
/// A hand-written `asJson` in the class body wins over the provided one
/// (ADR 0127 §3a).
///
/// ## Caching, inheritance, nil and secrets (BT-5191)
/// - `jsonMapping` runs **once per class**: the validated mapping is cached
///   and reused for every instance until a class is loaded, reloaded or
///   removed. It must answer the same mapping every time.
/// - A subclass inherits `asJson` and its parent's `class jsonMapping`. If it
///   declares fields of its own, `asJson` raises a `user_error` rather than
///   leave them off silently: override `class jsonMapping`, typically as
///   `super jsonMapping |> mapField: #extra`, or as `super jsonMapping` to
///   keep them off on purpose.
/// - A nil field is emitted as `null`; build the mapping with `omittingNil`
///   to leave such keys out.
/// - On an Actor, a mapped `secretState` slot without a converter is emitted
///   as `"[redacted]"`. See `JsonMapping` for the details.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// Value subclass: Issue
///   uses: JsonMappable
///   field: issueId = ""
///   field: title = ""
///
///   class jsonMapping -> JsonMapping =>
///     JsonMapping new
///       |> mapField: #issueId to: "issue_id"
///       |> mapField: #title
/// ```
Protocol define: JsonMappable
  extending: JsonRepresentable
  /// Required — the wire schema for instances of the using class.
  class jsonMapping -> JsonMapping

  /// The mapped Dictionary for the receiver.
  asJson -> Dictionary => (JsonMapping forClass: self class) encode: self
